# Rust build artifacts.
#
# `target/` is machine-generated, architecture-specific, and enormous — a full workspace
# build here is several gigabytes. Nothing in it belongs in history, and committing it
# would make every clone unusable.
/target/

# The research scratch workspaces.
#
# `.research/probe/` is a throwaway Cargo workspace built to verify crate versions and
# subprocess kill semantics; it carries its own `target/` and is not part of the product.
# The findings it produced are kept as the reports and data beside it.
.research/probe/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local configuration and credentials. A harness reads its key from the environment, but
# a stray local file must never be the thing that publishes one.
.env
*.local.toml

# Jujutsu's working state is not tracked; `.jj/` is written by `jj git init` itself and
# is already listed in its own ignore file, so it is named here only for clarity.
/.jj/
